meta { name: Contact details respect the opt-in, type: http, seq: 3 }
get { url: {{publicBase}}/authors/{{techAuthor}}, body: none, auth: none }
headers { X-Tenant-Key: {{techTenantKey}} }
docs {
  Verifies the contact opt-in.

  With `contact_public = true` (the local seed), `email` and `telegram` are
  populated. Set it false and re-run — both must become null while `quote`
  and `name` stay:

    UPDATE authors SET contact_public = false WHERE username = 'mara-okonkwo';

  NOTE: Kong caches public GETs for 60s (proxy-cache, see
  infrastructure/kong/kong.template.yml). Add a cache-busting query param
  or wait out the TTL, or you will see the previous body and think the
  opt-in is broken. It is not — this cost an afternoon once already.
}
